From b8921f753f729fbc0d32563acd60a998ab3fbf58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <a@b.c>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:10:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] bgmtl: perf2 line: record vs submit, frame-gap p95, GEM
 allocs per command buffer

One more line a second next to perf:/frames:/texpool: (same flag, /private/var/tmp/bgmtl.perf; nothing
runs when it is absent but a cached flag test per call):

  perf2: record R ms (draw D = X us/draw, bind B, bytes Y, pass P) of encode E ms, submit S ms;
         frame gap p50 A ms p95 B ms (n); per cbuf: a GEM allocs M MB, f frees, i images;
         mempool H hits M misses N MB held

- record: time inside this library's own recording calls (bgDraw incl. chl's binding flush and Turnip's
  vkCmd*, chlTextureFor on binds, setBytes, chl_render_begin), two clock reads per call when the flag is on.
  "encode" in the existing line runs from the first encoder to the commit and so also holds CoreAnimation's
  own work between calls: encode minus record is what this library does not own. This is the number that
  says where the 100-200 us/draw of production goes (library or CoreAnimation) before anything else is built.
- submit: commit -> flushed. There is no deferred replay in this runtime (commands go straight into the
  VkCommandBuffer), so this is the whole "replay" cost.
- frame gap: commit-to-commit intervals under 250 ms, p50 and p95 (src/bg_perfstat.h, tested on a host by
  test/bg_perfstat_test.c).
- GEM allocs / MB / frees / images per command buffer from chl_get_stats, and the bucketed memory pool's
  hits/misses/held (all zero with the pool off).

Not compiled (Objective-C, needs the iOS SDK; the percentile helper is compiled and tested on a host).

